# Data-collection control, sent by the teleop operator's buttons to a
# recorder node that may live on a different machine.
#
# The request carries a command and nothing else. Naming episodes,
# attaching metadata and deciding what is on disk are all the recorder's
# business -- the caller is a set of buttons and knows none of it.
#
# The recorder owns the state machine and is the single source of truth:
# a command that does not apply to its current state is rejected with
# success=false rather than silently changing anything. The caller is not
# expected to track state -- it reacts to RecorderStatus instead.

# START : begin a new episode.                    IDLE            -> RECORDING
# STOP  : end recording, keep the data buffered.  RECORDING       -> PENDING
# SAVE  : commit to storage. From RECORDING this  RECORDING/PENDING -> IDLE
#         also stops first, so a good demo ends
#         with a single press.
# DELETE: discard. From RECORDING or PENDING this RECORDING/PENDING -> IDLE
#         drops the buffered episode; from IDLE   IDLE            -> IDLE
#         it deletes the most recently saved one,
#         so an accidental SAVE can be undone.
#         How far back that undo reaches is the
#         recorder's policy.
uint8 START  = 0
uint8 STOP   = 1
uint8 SAVE   = 2
uint8 DELETE = 3

uint8 command
---
# false when the command did not apply to the recorder's state (nothing
# to save, nothing left to undo) or when storage failed. Not an error to
# log loudly -- the operator pressing SAVE twice is normal.
bool success

# Human-readable reason, always populated on failure.
string message

# The episode the recorder acted on: the id it generated for a START, or
# the one it resolved a DELETE to. Empty if the command touched no
# episode. Informational only -- it is here so the operator can see which
# episode a button press affected, not for the caller to send back.
string episode_id

# The recorder's state after handling this command, using the constants
# in RecorderStatus. Lets a caller stay in sync without waiting for the
# next status message.
uint8 state